---
import CalculatorLayout from "@/layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro"

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is a healthy BMI range?",
    a: "For most adults, a BMI between 18.5 and 24.9 is considered the healthy range. Below 18.5 is classed as underweight and 25 or above as overweight. BMI is a general screening tool, not a diagnosis.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does BMI work for athletes?",
    a: "Not always. BMI does not distinguish muscle from fat, so very muscular people may show a high BMI while having low body fat. Use it as one data point alongside other measures.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is BMI accurate for children?",
    a: "This calculator is intended for adults. Children and teenagers use age- and sex-specific BMI percentile charts instead of fixed categories.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should I use BMI to make health decisions?",
    a: "BMI is a rough screening estimate only. It is not a substitute for advice from a qualified healthcare professional who can consider your full situation.",
  },
]
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="BMI Calculator — Body Mass Index (Metric & Imperial)"
  description="Calculate your Body Mass Index (BMI) from height and weight in metric or imperial units. Free, private, and instant — with an explanation of the BMI formula."
  heading="BMI Calculator"
  intro="Enter your height and weight to estimate your Body Mass Index and see which standard weight category it falls into."
  slug="bmi"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <div slot="tool" class="tool">
    <div class="unit-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Measurement system">
      <button type="button" data-unit="metric" aria-pressed="true">Metric</button>
      <button type="button" data-unit="imperial" aria-pressed="false">Imperial</button>
    </div>

    <form novalidate data-calc>
      <div data-metric>
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="height-cm">Height (cm)</label>
            <input id="height-cm" name="heightCm" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="50" max="272" step="0.1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="height-cm" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="weight-kg">Weight (kg)</label>
            <input id="weight-kg" name="weightKg" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="10" max="500" step="0.1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="weight-kg" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div data-imperial hidden>
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="height-ft">Height (ft)</label>
            <input id="height-ft" name="heightFt" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="1" max="8" step="1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="height-ft" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="height-in">Height (in)</label>
            <input id="height-in" name="heightIn" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="11.9" step="0.1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="height-in" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="weight-lb">Weight (lb)</label>
            <input id="weight-lb" name="weightLb" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="20" max="1100" step="0.1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="weight-lb" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="actions">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Calculate BMI</button>
        <button type="reset" class="btn btn-ghost">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <div class="result" data-result hidden aria-live="polite">
      <p class="result-label">Your estimated BMI</p>
      <p class="result-value" data-value>—</p>
      <p><span class="badge" data-category></span></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Underweight: below 18.5</li>
        <li>Healthy weight: 18.5 – 24.9</li>
        <li>Overweight: 25 – 29.9</li>
        <li>Obese: 30 and above</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="formula">
    <p>Body Mass Index compares your weight to your height using this formula:</p>
    <p class="formula">BMI = weight (kg) ÷ [height (m)]²</p>
    <p>
      For imperial units, the equivalent formula multiplies by a conversion
      factor:
    </p>
    <p class="formula">BMI = 703 × weight (lb) ÷ [height (in)]²</p>
    <p>
      The result is grouped into standard categories set by the World Health
      Organization. Because BMI uses only height and weight, it cannot tell the
      difference between muscle and fat, so treat it as a general screening
      estimate.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="example">
    <p><strong>Person:</strong> 170 cm tall, weighing 68 kg.</p>
    <p>Convert height to metres: 170 cm = 1.70 m.</p>
    <p class="formula">BMI = 68 ÷ (1.70 × 1.70) = 68 ÷ 2.89 = 23.5</p>
    <p>
      A BMI of <strong>23.5</strong> falls within the healthy weight range of
      18.5 – 24.9.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>

<script>
  import { setupBmi } from "@/scripts/bmi"
  setupBmi()
</script>
